  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 202 AM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nUpper level ridging continues over the southern Plains, while an \nupper level trough tracks across the northern Plains. This will \ncontinue to support an active upper level pattern Sunday through \nearly week. Throughout the days, the upper level ridging should \ncontinue to support lower rain chances, with highs climbing into the \nmid 80s to mid 90s. Again, highs for early September are right \naround 84 to 85 degrees, so this looks to remain warmer than \naverage. With the fairly active upper level pattern, expect near \ndaily chances of rain each evening into the overnight hours. At this \ntime, the severe risk remains uncertain. \n\nMid to late week, stronger upper level ridging is expected to be the \ndominant feature. This will support warmer than average temperatures \ncontinuing through the end of the week, with highs potentially \nremaining in the 90s across the region. This stronger upper level \nridging is also expected to limit precipitation chances through the \nend of the week.",
